## Requirements

### Functional Requirements

- **FR-001**: System MUST allow users to create a supplier order.
- **FR-002**: System MUST allow users to record the supplier/manufacturer associated with a supplier order.
- **FR-003**: System MUST allow users to record the customer number for a supplier order.
- **FR-004**: System MUST allow users to record the order date.
- **FR-005**: System MUST allow users to record a P.O. number.
- **FR-006**: System MUST allow users to record products associated with an order.
- **FR-007**: Each order product MUST support a SKU, description, number of cases, price, and total.
- **FR-008**: System MUST allow users to create shipment records.
- **FR-009**: A shipment MUST support a shipped-to address.
- **FR-010**: A shipment MUST support a shipped-from address.
- **FR-011**: System MUST allow users to record the customer number associated with a shipment.
- **FR-012**: System MUST allow users to record the shipped date.
- **FR-013**: System MUST allow users to record the P.O. number associated with a shipment.
- **FR-014**: System MUST allow users to record the driver associated with a shipment.
- **FR-015**: Shipment products MUST support a SKU, description, quantity, price, and total.
- **FR-016**: System MUST allow users to record a delivery date.
- **FR-017**: System MUST allow users to record who received the shipment.
- **FR-018**: System MUST allow users to record an authorized-by value for a supplier order.
- **FR-019**: System MUST allow users to record the order date associated with the supplier order.
- **FR-020**: System MUST NOT allow a supplier order or shipment to be saved when required identifying information is missing.

---

## Assumptions

- The system will be used by warehouse personnel to manage supplier orders and shipments.
- A supplier order is associated with a supplier/manufacturer.
- A shipment can contain one or more products.
- A product can be identified by a SKU.
- The P.O. number can be used to associate an order with a shipment.
- The system will store the information represented on the provided Supplier Order Form and Bill of Lading.
- User authentication and authorization are not defined by the provided documents and are therefore not included in this feature.
- Inventory quantity tracking, automatic stock adjustments, and warehouse-location tracking are not defined by the provided documents and are not included in this feature.
- Payment processing is not defined by the provided documents and is not included.
- Automated shipping or delivery scheduling is not defined by the provided documents and is not included.

---

## Edge Cases

- Empty required field → System MUST identify the missing information and prevent the record from being saved.
- Duplicate P.O. number → System MUST identify that the P.O. number already exists rather than silently creating an unintended duplicate.
- Invalid quantity → System MUST reject a quantity that is not a valid positive value.
- Invalid price → System MUST reject a price that is not a valid monetary value.
- Missing SKU → System MUST prevent a product record from being saved without a SKU when the SKU is required.
- Missing shipment destination → System MUST prevent a shipment from being saved without required destination information.
- Missing driver → System MUST identify missing driver information when the driver is required for a shipment.
- Missing receiving information → System MUST allow the shipment to remain incomplete if receiving information has not yet been provided.
- Shipment without an associated P.O. number → System MUST identify the missing P.O. number when the P.O. number is required to associate the shipment with an order.

